{
 "what": "Decode of twitter.json as CBOR (402814 bytes) into the native values of five languages.",
 "why": "The binding of a language takes most of the time of a decode. This run compares four ways to hand the items to a binding.",
 "how": "push: the library calls one function of the binding per item (tag_invoke). push_key_hook: the same, and a text string that is a map key goes to map_key_decode, where the binding reuses one value per key. tape_build: the library writes a flat list of the items, and the binding builds its values from the list. tape_build_keys: the same, and the binding reuses one value per key. Two binaries per language, run in turn, five rounds, each with 5 repetitions in random order. A cell is the median of 25 repetitions in MiB per second. The spread of the 25 repetitions is the noise floor; no twin binary was built.",
